Test (ubuntu-24.04 / specification) shard 1/4	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-22T08:32:31.0867162Z   left: "## How to make tea\n\n1. Put fresh water into a kettle. If you're just making a cup of tea, pour about 1.5 times as much water as you need to fill the cup. — wikiHow (CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, sha256 6664c1741db7)\n2. Heat the water in your kettle until it comes to a boil. — wikiHow (CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, sha256 6664c1741db7)\n3. Microwave the water if you don't have a kettle or stove. — wikiHow (CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, sha256 6664c1741db7)\n4. Give the water a good stir before using it to make sure the heat distributes evenly. — wikiHow (CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, sha256 6664c1741db7)\n5. Pour a little water into the teapot or cup to preheat it. — wikiHow (CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, sha256 6664c1741db7)\n6. Place loose tea leaves or a tea bag into the teapot or cup. — wikiHow (CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, sha256 6664c1741db7)\n7. Or, place a strainer into the cup before you pour in the tea so that you can catch the leaves. — wikiHow (CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, sha256 6664c1741db7)\n8. If you like tea that has a stronger taste, feel free to add more leaves or an extra tea bag. — wikiHow (CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, sha256 6664c1741db7)\n9. Pour the hot water over the tea bags or leaves. — wikiHow (CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, sha256 6664c1741db7)\n10. Steep the tea according to the type of tea. — wikiHow (CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, sha256 6664c1741db7)\n11. Strain the tea leaves or remove the tea bags. — wikiHow (CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, sha256 6664c1741db7)\n12. Feel free to compost your tea bags or leaves once you've finished making tea. — wikiHow (CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, sha256 6664c1741db7)\n\n### Sources\n- github — unbound_template (0 page(s), 0 step(s)): https://api.github.com/repos/{owner}/{repo}/readme\n- wikifunctions — unbound_template (0 page(s), 0 step(s)): https://www.wikifunctions.org/w/api.php?action=query&format=json&formatversion=2&list=wikilambdasearch_functions&wikilambdasearch_functions_search={query}&wikilambdasearch_functions_language={language}&wikilambdasearch_functions_limit=5\n- wikihow — contributed (1 page(s), 12 step(s)): https://www.wikihow.com/api.php?action=parse&page=Make-Tea&prop=text%7Csections%7Cdisplaytitle&format=json&origin=*\naction=opensearch&search=make%20tea&limit=5&format=json&origin=*\norder=desc&sort=relevance&q=make%20tea&site=stackoverflow&filter=withbody\naction=query&list=search&srsearch=make%20tea&srlimit=5&format=json&origin=*\n- wikihow → https://www.wikihow.com/api.php?action=parse&page=Make-Tea&prop=text%7Csections%7Cdisplaytitle&format=json&origin=* (CC BY-NC-SA 3.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/)\n\nBounds: max_depth=2 max_pages_per_service=4 max_services=4 max_items=12 max_capture_age_seconds=5184000"
